# The bomb: 240 dormant, 241 dormant and the player has her notes, 242 rigged, 243 disarmed.
{240}{}{The bomb? I had the access plate off once! It's mostly missing a doohickey, so it's probably safe. Probably! The ticking is just it thinking things over.}
{241}{}{You've got my notes! Page three is the important one. And five. Actually, don't skip four either.}
{242}{}{It's humming! Somebody put a brand new part in the empty socket. I'd love to shake their hand, and then stand a long way off. It could be pulled out again. Carefully!}
{243}{}{Dead as a doornail! I checked. Twice. The second time with a hammer.}
{244}{}{You opened a live bomb. Tell me you wrote it down.}
{245}{}{Did you keep notes? I could use them.}
{246}{}{Probably safe?}
{247}{}{Let me ask you something else.}

{250}{}{Of course I wrote it down! Diagrams and everything. Here, take them, I know it all by heart. If a wire isn't in the picture, don't lick it.}
{251}{}{I sure did! Fifty and they're yours. Paper is dear around here: I had to peel that off a wall and iron it.}
{252}{}{Fifty. Here.}
{253}{}{Twenty-five. It's wallpaper with a drawing on it.}
{254}{}{Too rich for me.}
{255}{}{A pleasure! Follow the diagram and you'll be fine. If you aren't fine, come back and tell me which page was wrong.}
{256}{}{Wallpaper with a very GOOD drawing on it! But all right, twenty-five. You haggle like a caravan man.}
{257}{}{Oh. You don't have it on you. That's all right! Come back when you do. The bomb isn't going anywhere. Probably.}
{258}{}{I'm ninety percent sure. Well, eighty. The number isn't the important part! The important part is that it hasn't gone off yet, and that's a very good record.}
{259}{}{Me buy boom pictures. [Give her $50.]}
{260}{}{Yes! Big boom ball! Well, big quiet ball. I drew pictures of its insides. You can have them for fifty shiny coins. Pictures are good. No reading at all!}
{261}{}{Me no want.}
{262}{}{There you go! Red line bad, blue line good. Or is it... no. Yes. Red bad. Have fun!}
{263}{}{That's not fifty. That's... hold on. That's a button and some lint. Come back with fifty coins, all right? Fifty. Both hands, five times.}

# Asked what else would help with the bomb: 266 she lends her tools, 267 the player has tools already, 268 for few words.
{266}{}{Close is good! Close means the notes work! Were you poking it with a knife? Here, my spare tools. A loan! Bring them back if there's still a town. And clear your head first: Doc Church sells Mentats.}
{267}{}{Close is good! And you have proper tools, so it isn't your hands. Then it's your head! Mentats. Doc Church sells them, and there may be a few rattling about town. They make the wires hold still.}
{268}{}{Oh, it bit you? With your bare hands? Here: twisty stick. It goes in the little cross holes. Bring it back! And ask the doctor for the thinking candy. Thinking candy first, then twisty stick.}

{265}{}{Lost them? Oh, don't worry, I make copies of everything since the fire! Here. This one is a little singed, but the dangerous parts are all still readable.}

# The survival guide: one question, answered once.
{270}{}{The Wasteland Survival Guide! Everything a person needs to not die out there. I need field data. Quick one: you're three days from water and you find a puddle that glows a little. What do you do?}
{271}{}{Drink it. My stomach has survived worse.}
{272}{}{Boil it, strain it through charcoal, drink it slowly.}
{273}{}{Bottle it and sell it to the Children of Atom.}
{274}{}{Ask me another time.}
{275}{}{Me drink glow juice! Yum.}
{276}{}{Straight down! That goes in the 'Do Not' column, with your name beside it to show it can be survived. Take these stimpaks, for when your stomach finds out.}
{277}{}{Charcoal! Of course! That's a whole paragraph. Here, have a RadAway, for the puddles that haven't read my book.}
{278}{}{That's not survival, that's commerce! ...Which is chapter nine, actually. Have some Mentats. You clearly get ideas, and these make more of them.}
{279}{}{Subject drinks it. Unprompted! And smiling! Oh, this is going in the book. Here, a RadAway. No, don't eat the bag. Well. Eat it slowly.}
{280}{}{Chapter one is finished, thanks to you! Chapter two needs somebody to get bitten by something. No hurry! Think it over.}

{285}{}{That's my mercenary! He came in with a caravan and I pay him to stand there. He doesn't care for the experiments. He says a man can only be set on fire so many times. I asked how many. He won't help me find out.}
{286}{}{He was my mercenary. He never did tell me his name, so I wrote 'The Grump' on the marker. He'd have hated that. That's how I know it's right.}

{290}{}{You did? It's really dead? That's wonderful! And a tiny bit sad. I had so many more things to try on it. Ten percent off everything for the hero of Megaton! I'd make it fifteen, but I already painted the sign.}

# Lucy West's letter when the caravan trader is dead: 295 the player has it, 296 the paper is gone.
{295}{}{Oh no, poor Harith! And he was so lucky, too. Leave the letter with me! Crow's caravan is due, and he owes me for a toaster. It'll go north with him, no charge. Mail is important!}
{296}{}{Oh no, poor Harith! And you've lost the letter as well? Then tell me who it's for and I'll write it out fresh for Crow's caravan. I do a very good 'Dear Mother'.}

